{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"spell_barkskin","model_identifier":"spell_barkskin","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# spell_barkskin\n\nGrovesinger barkskin: pale bark plates that grow over a protected ally's chest, back, shoulders and arms, then flake away. A light shell fitted to the humanoid baseline (60 u worker): it uses the same bones and pivots (`root > hips > torso`, `arm_upper_*`, `arm_lower_*`), so the game copies the unit's bone transforms onto it each frame and scales it to the unit's height (1.07 for elves at 1.9 m, 0.71 for 1.2 m goblins).\n\n- Bounds (first set): x -12..12, y 31..51.5, z -5.5..5 units (0.68 x 0.58 x 0.30 m). Origin at the base centre, front faces -Z.\n- Texture: 32 x 32, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering; every visible face has its own region painted with its material (identical faces share one). No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: 20.\n\n## Hit box\n\n- none (an effect on a unit; the unit keeps its own box)\n\n## Clips\n\n| clip | length (s) | loop | what moves |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `grow` | 0.8 | once | plates swell out of nothing, chest first, then shoulders, upper arms and bracers (overshoot to 1.15, settle at 1.0); holds the full shell at the end |\n| `flake` | 1.0 | once | plates crack off one after another, drift outward and fall about 10 u, tumbling, shrinking to nothing by 1.0 s |\n\n- Rest pose = the full shell, so the game shows the rest pose while the spell lasts.\n- Glowing cubes (`glow_*`): glow_sap_chest, glow_sap_bracer_r, glow_sap_bracer_l (thin pale-green sap seams).\n\n## Notes\n\n- Bright simple shapes; every lit cube is named `glow_*` (flat colours; the game may scale, spin and fade them). No particles or lights in the file.\n- Made by the model thread (review of batch 2): the bot's batches left this wishlist entry out.\n"},"resoluti